<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Multi-Party Negotiating Forum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1993">1993</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Multi-Party Negotiating Forum was the body that negotiated the end of apartheid in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> in 1993, after the breakdown of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/convention-for-a-democratic-south-africa">CODESA</a>. Meeting at Kempton Park, it brought together 26 parties and organisations, survived the assassination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chris-hani">Chris Hani</a>, and agreed the interim constitution and the date of the first democratic election, 27 April 1994.</p></div>
